dhp105:1 starts: neither a deva nor gandhabba,
dhp105:2 starts: nor a Mara banded with Brahmas,
dhp105:3 starts: could turn that triumph
dhp105:4 starts: back into defeat.
dhp112:1 starts: And better than a hundred years
dhp112:2 starts: lived apathetic & unenergetic, is
dhp112:3 starts: one day
dhp112:4 starts: lived energetic & firm.
dhp131:1 starts: Whoever takes a rod
dhp131:2 starts: to harm living beings desiring ease,
dhp131:3 starts: when he himself is looking for ease,
dhp131:4 starts: meets with no ease after death.
dhp132:1 starts: Whoever doesn’t take a rod
dhp132:2 starts: to harm living beings desiring ease,
dhp132:3 starts: when he himself is looking for ease,
dhp132:4 starts: meets with ease after death.
dhp143:1 starts: Who in the world
dhp143:2 starts: is a man constrained by conscience,
dhp143:3 starts: who awakens to censure
dhp143:4 starts: like a fine stallion to the whip?
dhp106:1 starts: You could,
dhp106:2 starts: month by month,
dhp106:3 starts: or
dhp106:4 starts: to one person,
dhp106:5 starts: Better than a hundred years of sacrifices
dhp106:6 starts: would that act of homage be.
dhp107:1 starts: You could, for a hundred years,
dhp107:2 starts: live in a forest
dhp107:3 starts: or
dhp107:4 starts: to one person,
dhp107:5 starts: Better than a hundred years of sacrifices
dhp107:6 starts: would that act of homage be.
dhp110:1 starts: Better than a hundred years
dhp110:2 starts: lived without virtue, uncentered, is
dhp110:3 starts: one day
dhp110:4 starts: lived by a virtuous person
dhp111:1 starts: And better than a hundred years
dhp111:2 starts: lived undiscerning, uncentered, is
dhp111:3 starts: one day
dhp111:4 starts: lived by a discerning person
dhp114:1 starts: And better than a hundred years
dhp114:2 starts: lived without seeing
dhp114:3 starts: one day
dhp114:4 starts: lived seeing
dhp123:1 starts: Like a merchant with a small
dhp123:2 starts: but well-laden caravan
dhp123:3 starts: –a dangerous road,
dhp123:4 starts: like a person who loves life
dhp124:1 starts: If there’s no wound on the hand,
dhp124:2 starts: that hand can hold poison.
dhp124:3 starts: Poison won’t penetrate
dhp124:4 starts: There’s no evil
dhp134:1 starts: If, like a flattened metal pot
dhp134:2 starts: you don’t resound,
dhp134:3 starts: you’ve attained an Unbinding;
dhp134:4 starts: in you there’s found
dhp135:1 starts: As a cowherd with a rod
dhp135:2 starts: drives cows to the field,
dhp135:3 starts: so aging & death
dhp135:4 starts: drive the life
dhp136:1 starts: When doing evil deeds,
dhp136:2 starts: the fool is oblivious.
dhp136:3 starts: The dullard
dhp136:4 starts: is tormented
dhp140:1 starts: houses burned down.
dhp140:2 starts: At the break-up of the body
dhp140:3 starts: this one with no discernment,
dhp140:4 starts: reappears in
dhp149:1 starts: On seeing these bones
dhp149:2 starts: like gourds in the fall,
dhp149:3 starts: pigeon-gray:
dhp149:4 starts: what delight?
dhp150:1 starts: A city made of bones,
dhp150:2 starts: plastered over with flesh & blood,
dhp150:3 starts: whose hidden treasures are:
dhp150:4 starts: pride & contempt,
